; AI A/B test settings for C builds (fork branch claude/ab-c1, from c7c_flags on).
; Copy to Documents\My Games\Sid Meier's Civilization 5\AIABTest.ini. A test game reads it once, when it
; starts, and saves the settings with the game, so changing it never affects a game already running.
; No file, or an empty line, means the bundle: the same AI as c7c.
;
; Flag names (any case): WidePlans BoxedIn LongWide BoxedInWar TimingAttack SiegeTechs SiegeBook
; DeclareTiming GrowthTech AqueductValue GreedyArmyCap GreedyBook GreedyTarget CanWin ClosedBorders
; Topic flags, only in their branch's builds until they pass (and off in the bundle):
;   ab-ai-economy-latest (ai/economy): SettlersFirst SettlerOverlap DiploPolicyValue
;   ab-ai-war-latest (ai/war): SiegeStay SiegePosture DeclareAtBorder
; A name the installed build doesn't know goes to AIABTest_errors.txt and is ignored.
; Lists: names separated by commas or spaces; "bundle" = the c7c ideas (every flag above but LongWide,
; GreedyArmyCap and the topic flags),
; "all", "none", and "-Name" takes a flag out again. Unknown names go to AIABTest_errors.txt next to this file.
;
; Examples:
;   Fixes = CanWin               group c runs only CanWin (an SPRT test of one idea)
;   Fixes = bundle, -CanWin      the bundle without CanWin (ablation)
;   Fixes = none                 c runs nothing: an A/A game that measures the split's bias
;   Screen = SiegeBook, CanWin   each listed flag is on for a random half of the AI civs (screening)
;
; Paired games: Run-Games.ps1 writes this file itself before every game (its -Fixes and -Screen). For the second
; game of a pair it adds Flip = 1 (groups swapped) and the first game's MapSeed, SyncSeed and Player<i> lines,
; copied from AIABTest_lastgame.ini, which every test game writes when it starts.
[ABTest]
Fixes = bundle
Screen =
Flip = 0

; Difficulty: the game's difficulty (a HandicapInfos type), whatever Civ's setup screen remembers. Builds from
; fork commit fdad60d on; older builds ignore it. Run-Games.ps1 writes its -ExpectDifficulty here.
Difficulty = HANDICAP_KING
